{"name":"Sea Creature","hex":"#00586d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"},{"term":"creature","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thing or being that has been created; a creation. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A human."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creature"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marine life","blocks":[{"text":"Marine life, which is also known as sea life or ocean life, refers to all the marine organisms that live in salt water habitats, or ecological communities that encompass all aquatic animals, plants, algae, fungi, protists, single-celled microorganisms and associated viruses living in the saline water of marine habitats, either the sea water of marginal seas and oceans, or the brackish water of coastal wetlands, lagoons, estuaries and inland seas. As of 2023, more than 242,000 marine species have been documented, and perhaps two million marine species are yet to be documented. On average, researches describe about 2,300 new marine species each year. The study of marine life spans into multiple fields, which is primarily marine biology, as well as biological oceanography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Orca_porpoising.jpg/330px-Orca_porpoising.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marine_life","wikidata":"Q1230015"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Composition_of_seawater.jpg/330px-Composition_of_seawater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Composition_of_seawater.jpg/330px-Composition_of_seawater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Composition of seawater. Quantities in relation to 1 kg or 1 litre of sea water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComposition_of_seawater.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Collapsed_tree_labels_simplified.png/500px-Collapsed_tree_labels_simplified.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Collapsed_tree_labels_simplified.png/500px-Collapsed_tree_labels_simplified.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Evolutionary tree showing the divergence of modern species from their common ancestor in the centre.[58] The three domains are coloured, with bacteria blue, archaea green and eukaryotes red.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACollapsed_tree_labels_simplified.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Tree_of_Living_Organisms_2.png/500px-Tree_of_Living_Organisms_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Tree_of_Living_Organisms_2.png/1280px-Tree_of_Living_Organisms_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o